From f652850256351ba5fa483d1797c1a4af7d977960 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 23:18:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02209/11362] [outer-loop] cross-game value transfer BUILT;
 honest A/B: generic features too weak for hard tail (wa30)

Pooled r11l+ls20+lp85 trajectories -> game-agnostic frame features -> normalized
steps-to-go -> a transferred verifier wired into v3. A/B on wa30: cross-game verifier
does NOT help (both no-advance, 66s vs 77s). Generic grid features don't transfer to
wa30's game-specific progress signal -- mirrors the domain-bound-verifier finding.
CONCLUSION: deep/sparse hard tail needs per-game RE or a richer learned representation,
not generic transfer. Calibrated ARC strategy recorded in the registry.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
